<!DOCTYPE html><html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
<head>
<title>IMGPNT: Creation or updating of PNT files from a monoband or multiband raster</title>
<meta content="text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1" http-equiv="Content-Type"/></head>
<body>
<!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent al titol de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<h1><span id="wpstitol"/></h1>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent titol de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->

<!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<span id="wpsopcions"/>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->

<p align="justify">In the multiband case, the values of the different bands in different fields will be stored in the registry of each point. If the raster file is a categorical band, the name of the corresponding category will be stored. If it is the case that the value of a cell in a monoband file or in the different layers in a multiband is a NODATA value, no point will be created.</p>

<p align="justify">For the execution of this application, a selection of the values of the cells of the input raster can be made. It also allows you to add new points to a pre-existing point file, that is, if the output file already exists and contains points, the application's execution will add new points extracted from the input raster. If it happens that the output file is in a different reference system than the input raster, the created points will be transformed to the reference system of the output file.</p>  
  
<p align="justify">The input file must be a raster in IMG format and the data type can be any of those supported by MiraMon (<a href="..%5Cmm32%5CAP1.htm"> see the formats supported by the MiraMon </a>).</p>
  <hr/>

  <exclusiva>
<!-- Aquí inicia la part corresponent a la sintaxi de miramon. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
